{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And know that ויאמר למך.</b> [It is] later in the pericope, and I have already mentioned two like it, and like it: \"ויקח האיש נזם זהב\" (Genesis 24:22), and likewise \"אמר אל בני ישראל אתם עם קשה ערף\" (Exodus 33:5), and likewise ואתחנן (Deuteronomy 3:23). And the reason is as the Sages said: that Adah and Zillah refrained, for they feared to bear children because they would be seventh from Cain and would be killed or die. Therefore Lamech said to his wives: I am truly the seventh, and if a man who is grown or a child wounds me and makes me a bruise — I killed him, and the word הרגתי is in place of אהרוג, and like it: \"נתתי כסף השדה\" (Genesis 23:13), \"אשר לקחתי מיד האמורי\" (Genesis 48:22), and many like them." "And if Cain's vengeance is sevenfold, Lamech's is seventy-seven, because he killed in error and I did not kill. And the meaning of what he said to his wives: the decree against Cain has already been annulled — and in truth the children of Lamech and all his seed died in the Flood, and no remnant of the violence of his brother was left to Cain."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The word אחריהם in the closing formula I read as אחריכם ('after you'), plural feminine, addressing the wives throughout; the alternative singular reading 'after you' (אחריך) seems less likely given the plural addressees."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:25.165434916Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}